{
  "form_version": "2026-09-26.1",
  "title": "Near-expiry stock: practitioner feedback",
  "intro": "Five minutes on how near-expiry stock is handled in your business today, and what you think of Taal. There are no right answers. Only the first two questions and the consent box at the end are required.",
  "estimated_minutes": 5,
  "taal_description": [
    "Taal looks at every lot of perishable stock in a store and works out which ones will not sell before their date, or before the online sell-by deadline.",
    "For each of those lots it proposes a targeted offer to the customers most likely to buy, with the expected margin stated up front, and a person approves it before anything is sent.",
    "It holds back a random group of customers who get no offer, so the result is measured against them instead of guessed."
  ],
  "landing_url": "/",
  "consent_statement": "We store your answers to understand how retailers handle near-expiry stock and to support the evidence in our project submission. Answers are kept for up to 12 months and then deleted. Your name and contact details, if you give them, are stored separately from your answers, are used only to arrange a pilot, and are never included in any report. You can ask us to delete your response at any time by quoting the reference shown after you submit. Taking part is voluntary.",
  "thank_you": "Thank you. Your response has been recorded.",
  "sections": [
    {
